cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "Bilingual Hate-Speech Detection (EN/PT): classical vs. transformer models"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible, leakage-safe study comparing classical models (TF-IDF and multilingual
  sentence embeddings) with transformers (XLM-RoBERTa, BERTimbau, BERTweet) for binary
  hate-speech classification in English and Portuguese, with calibration, identity-term
  bias, cross-lingual transfer analyses, and a deployable inference API.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Venancio da Silva"
    given-names: "Isabela"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0156-7837"
    affiliation: "University of São Paulo, School of Public Health (FSP-USP), LABDAPS"
date-released: "2026-07-27"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/isasaade-23/hate-speech-nlp-en-pt"
keywords:
  - hate speech detection
  - natural language processing
  - multilingual NLP
  - Portuguese
  - text classification
  - transformers
  - cross-lingual transfer
  - model calibration
  - algorithmic bias
